$ git fetch --all origin
fetch all=true remote=origin
$ git remote add origin https://example.com/r
remote add origin https://example.com/r
$ git remote show
remote show
$ git remote dry-run
remote dry-run
$ git init
init
$ git -V
git 2.0.1
$ git 
refused: []
Track changes

Usage: git [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  fetch          Download objects
  remote         Manage remotes
  init           Create a repository
  help           Print help for git or one of its commands

Options:
  -V, --version  Print the version
  -h, --help     Print help

See the manual for more.
